From 78a8286686ffc8b76933823bdddc72f49e92b05d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:33:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] MLT_NO_THREADS: the avformat module on the calling thread

Without threads (mlt_threads_disabled):
- the avformat producer starts no packets_worker; packets_read_inline()
  reads packets as the decoder needs them, as the worker would have;
- decoders and encoders whose threads property asks for the default (0)
  get one thread, not FFmpeg's automatic count, and so do libavfilter
  graphs (mlt_avformat_thread_count, mlt_avformat_graph_threads);
- the avformat and null consumers do all their work inside
  mlt_consumer_start, which returns when they have finished;
- melt therefore reports progress, and passes on a stop asked for by
  SIGINT or SIGTERM, from the consumer-frame-show event.
---
